{"author":{"id":"86dc3c885e4fa466d19699d4a5e74c240f1c9d6b23f4e62ea2d2d8e359bd1711"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789490221,"nonce":"7n6/9tu3nEFL2ZLvL64syv72u1M=","title":"Add the portable one-document workflow","message":"## Parent\n\ngit-bug issue `60b2077` — PRD: GIC v0.9 workshop environment\n\n## What to build\n\nAdd one active-document behavior through a shared document model and a portable browser adapter. Students can open a `.gic` file, edit it, explicitly download/save it, use Save As semantics, and receive dirty-state and discard protection without persistent browser filesystem handles.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] Only one source document is active at a time.\n- [ ] Opening another source or replacing dirty work requires explicit discard confirmation.\n- [ ] Open accepts a real local `.gic` file through portable browser input behavior.\n- [ ] Save and Save As produce a downloadable `.gic` file without storing a persistent filesystem handle.\n- [ ] Dirty state reflects source changes and clears only after the selected explicit save completes.\n- [ ] When enabled, format-on-save runs exactly once before explicit save; disabling the setting preserves the edited formatting.\n- [ ] Playwright covers open, edit, save, Save As, cancellation, and discard paths using real files/downloads.\n\n## Blocked by\n\n- git-bug issue `184f8de` — Replace the browser textarea with Monaco\n- git-bug issue `f4391b4` — Format GIC documents","files":null}]}